      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "I support this idea only because it makes sense. It would be a lot more optimized in some scenarios to use a physbone collider for avatar interactions for mesh/bone manipulation than to use a lot of contacts with a lot of parameters + animator layers and using specific shaders to achieve a similar effect. Using custom tags would help a lot in this regard.",
      "viewerReactions": null,
      "voteID": null
    }
  ],
  "companyID": "58c62e995865713647a7115d",
  "created": "2022-04-08T08:36:14.320Z",
  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "Only the PhysBone of the local player can interfere with a manually added VRCPhysBoneCollider.\nIf we could create a VRCPhysBoneCollider that can interfere between agreed players (like setting Collision Tags in Contact), the range of expression would be greatly expanded.\n手動で追加したVRCPhysBoneColliderに干渉できるのは、ローカルプレイヤーのPhysBoneのみです。\n（ContactでCollision Tagsを設定するように）合意したプレイヤー間で干渉できるVRCPhysBoneColliderができれば、表現の幅が大きく広がるのではないでしょうか。",
